    {
      "name": "Send Audit Email",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.gmail",
      "typeVersion": 2.1,
      "position": [
        2860,
        -200
      ],
      "webhookId": "223421c0-1e5b-44a2-917f-0dffd36d1653",
      "parameters": {
        "sendTo": "={{ $json.email }}",
        "subject": "=Quick fix for {{ $json.business_name }}'s mobile conversion drop?",
        "emailType": "html",
        "message": "=<p>Hi {{ $json.greeting_name }},</p>\n\n<p>I was reviewing a few local businesses in Chennai and looked at your website ({{ $json.domain }}).</p>\n\n<p>I ran Google's own Lighthouse performance test on it, on mobile. Your page takes <strong>{{ $json.speed_index }}</strong> to visibly load (Speed Index), and its mobile performance score is <strong>{{ $json.perf_score }}/100</strong>. Anything above 3 seconds usually means a big share of mobile visitors leave before they see your page, which also wastes your local SEO effort.</p>\n\n<p>I run <strong>Astra Nexora</strong>, a conversion optimisation and automation agency here in Tamil Nadu. We fix exactly these technical leaks without big-agency budgets.</p>\n\n<p>I've written down a 2-step fix for this speed problem. Are you open to a quick 10-minute call on {{ $json.call_day }} to go through it?</p>\n\n<p>Best regards,<br>\n<strong>S. Saktheeswaran</strong><br>\nFounder &amp; CEO, Astra Nexora<br>\n<a href=\"https://astranexora.netlify.app\">astranexora.netlify.app</a> · <a href=\"https://saktheeswaran.netlify.app\">saktheeswaran.netlify.app</a></p>\n\n<p style=\"color:#888;font-size:12px\">You can check the result yourself at pagespeed.web.dev. If this isn't useful, just reply \"no\" and I won't email again.</p>\n",
        "options": {
          "appendAttribution": false,
          "senderName": "S. Saktheeswaran"
        }
      },
      "id": "f0716bf5-c85b-5a03-b395-e0f6cb91f6c0"
    },
    {
      "name": "Mark Sent",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        3080,
        -200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Code node \"Mark Sent\" (Run Once for Each Item)\n// The Gmail node returns only the message id, so restore the lead data.\nreturn {\n  json: {\n    ...$('Pick Decision Maker').item.json,\n    status: 'sent',\n    note: 'gmail id ' + ($json.id || ''),\n  },\n};\n",
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem"
      },
      "id": "9bb54a55-7d3d-5174-b800-9b232ba7df94"
    },
